"""Huma Control Center: system service that turns off the keyboard light when idle.

The GNOME extension only runs while a session is open; on the login screen, the lock
screen and after logging out the light stayed on. This service runs as root from boot,
only reads keyboard and touchpad events (evdev), turns the light off after the set idle
time and restores the previous level on the first touch.
Between sunrise and sunset it starts with the light off: at boot, on login, on resume
from sleep and at sunrise (it can be turned on with Fn+F6 afterwards).

Ambient light (this laptop has no light sensor, it is measured with the camera:
huma-control-light; the camera light flashes briefly while measuring, nothing is measured
if the camera is open in another app; while a movie / full screen is playing the GNOME
extension leaves /run/user/<uid>/huma-control-pause, no measurement then, one
measurement once it ends):
  dark_turn_on     follow ambient light (to save power): on when dark, off when bright;
                   measured when returning from a break, 3 s after Fn+F6 and every
                   measure_interval_s seconds while someone is at the computer; turning off
                   in daytime does not apply in a dark room
  screen_auto      measure every measure_interval_s seconds while someone is at the computer
                   and when returning from a break; result in /run/huma-control/light.json,
                   the Huma Control Center GNOME extension sets the screen brightness
  battery_only     save power only on battery (default): on AC the light is not turned off
                   when idle, in daytime or when bright, the Fn+F6 choice is kept; it is
                   still turned on in the dark; measured at most every 10 minutes. Measured
                   right away when AC is unplugged, turned off if it is daytime.

Settings in /etc/huma-control/keyboard.json (written by Huma Control Center through
huma-control-helper):
  {"idle_timeout_s": 15, "off_in_daytime": true, "location": [latitude, longitude],
   "dark_turn_on": false, "dark_threshold": 20, "very_dark_threshold": 8, "screen_auto": false,
   "screen_sensitivity": 2, "measure_interval_s": 600, "osd": true, "battery_only": true,
   "sun_full": true, "sun_threshold": 1000, "screen_method": "stages",
   "screen_stages": [15, 30, 60, 80, 100], "presence": false, "presence_s": 60,
   "presence_camera": "auto"}
  Keyboard levels: below very_dark_threshold Bright (2), below dark_threshold Dim (1), above
  1.5 times dark_threshold Off; left alone in between.
  The helper writes the file (this service cannot write /etc: ProtectSystem=strict).

  huma-control-keyboard --validate   merge the settings on stdin with the current ones,
                                     validate, print the resulting JSON
"""
